      "side": 1,
      "message": "You shouldn\u0027t need to do this explicitly. If you got `EC_ERROR_NOT_POWERED`, then `vbus_mv` should already have this value, so you could combine the cases.\n\nAs noted below, you could go even further and do this regardless of the return value or pass `\u0026vbus_voltage_cache[chgnum]` directly into `get_vbus_voltage`, relying upon `get_vbus_voltage` to always assign a value that `configure_vbus_thresholds` can use. If you still wanted to log the I2C error informationally, you could do that in `get_vbus_voltage`.",
      "revId": "5ebd4bed29e0ff6e54e0a961d0c03dcf28f69a3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
